    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhile trying to upgrade the Alpine linux package to 12.5, many functional tests fail (locally and in CI) with the error Failed to --listen: invalid argument: \"T----\". Seemingly related PR: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40625\n\nRaw CI logs (x86_64): https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/brianleblanc98/aports/-/jobs/2534647/raw\n\nRaw CI logs (aarch64): https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/brianleblanc98/aports/-/jobs/2534639/raw\n\nRelevant PR on Alpine Linux aports repo: https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/merge_requests/109039\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nbuild() {\n\tlocal cmakeoptions=\n\tcase \"$CARCH\" in\n\t\tppc64le | riscv64 | s390x | loongarch64) cmakeoptions=\"-DPREFER_LUA=ON\" ;;\n\tesac\n\n\tcmake -B build -G Ninja \\\n\t\t-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=MinSizeRel \\\n\t\t-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr \\\n\t\t-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib \\\n\t\t-DENABLE_LTO=TRUE \\\n\t\t-DCMAKE_VERBOSE_MAKEFILE=TRUE \\\n\t\t-DENABLE_TRANSLATIONS=ON \\\n\t\t$cmakeoptions\n\tcmake --build build\n}\n\ncheck() {\n\t# Required by the unit tests but not set on the Alpine GitLab CI.\n\texport USER=\"$(id -un)\"\n\n\t# Without this, the temp directory for the tests exceeds the sun_path\n\t# buffer in sockaddr_un, causing test failures due to path trunctation.\n\texport XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/tmp\n\n\t# Needed to ensure that neovim finds the tree-parser grammars.\n\tln -Tfs /usr/lib/tree-sitter \"$builddir\"/runtime/parser\n\n\texport TEST_TIMEOUT=12000\n\n\tmsg \"Running unit tests\"\n\t# cmake --build build --target unittest\n\n\t# The functional tests are known to fail on 32-bit arches.\n\t# See: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/32230\n\tcase \"$CARCH\" in\n\tarm*|x86) return ;;\n\tesac\n\n\t# fails on x86_64\n\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS --filter-out quitting.swapfile.dialog.on.startup\"\n\t# https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/33911\n\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS --filter-out stdpath.*NVIM_APPNAME.relative.path\"\n\t# those appears to be flaky:\n\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS --filter-out put.command...register.special.tests.should.ring\"\n\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS --filter-out jobs.jobstop.*kills.entire.process.tree\"\n\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS --filter-out TUI.in.nvim_list_uis..,.sets.nvim_set_client_info\"\n\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS --filter-out tmpdir.disappeared\"\n\t# fails with 0.11.7\n\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS --filter-out API.nvim_get_runtime_file.can.find\"\n\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS --filter-out :write.converts.to.GB18030.with.iconv\"\n\n\tmsg \"Running functional tests\"\n\t# ensure we dont leak system config\n\tenv -i \\\n\t\tHOME=\"$PWD/.home\" \\\n\t\tXDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$PWD/.xdg-config\" \\\n\t\tXDG_DATA_HOME=\"$PWD/.xdg-data\" \\\n\t\tXDG_STATE_HOME=\"$PWD/.xdg-state\" \\\n\t\tXDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$PWD/.xdg-cache\" \\\n\t\tXDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/tmp \\\n\t\tTMPDIR=\"$PWD/build/Xtest_tmpdir\" \\\n\t\tPATH=\"$PATH\" \\\n\t\tTEST_SKIP_FRAGILE=1 \\\n\t\tTEST_ARGS=\"$TEST_ARGS\" \\\n\t\tTEST_FILE=test/functional/plugin/lsp_spec.lua \\\n\t\tcmake --build build --target functionaltest\n}\n\n```\n\nNote: unit tests are not run in this as they pass and only one `TEST_FILE` is used to save on build time, however many other test files fail with the same error.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nTests pass\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n12.5\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nAlpine linux edge, x86_64 and aarch64\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nn/a\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nn/a\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from source",
